																		SCP Early concept: the greatest artist
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/marquesigoo" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7003758); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7003758&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609315137" alt="marquesigoo" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7003758)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/marquesigoo" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7003758); return false;" >marquesigoo</a></span> <span class="odate time_1605232272 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">13 Nov 2020 01:51</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4817292">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights</strong>: Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type</strong>: SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch</strong>:This SCP is an unidentified being that has shown itself quite fascinated by human art, it regularly shape-shifts between 6 forms, each representing an art movement in history, these forms vary from a stoic Egyptian Pharaoh to a very surreal blob of energy that is a visual representation of the concept of &quot;Abstract&quot; the thing all of these instances share in common is the desire to produce a masterpiece, any damage to their art can and will be retaliated.</p>
<p>This SCP requests increasingly more and higher quality art supplies to make its own art, it went from being satisfied with paper and crayons to demanding the amount of paint equivalent of what would be needed to paint the Sistine Chapple.</p>
<p>This SCP wants to create art, if its art supplies are not provided quickly it will find a suitable replacement, by any means necessary, for example shaping a human bone enough to make it able to carve a hieroglyph on a wall.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">See&nbsp;more</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">See&nbsp;Less</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative</strong>: after the SCP is secured when it was shapeshifting and crying all the while obsessively staring at a painting in a museum, a particular incident will happen where the SCP freaked out about just not understanding humans and breaking its character of being a human that put him on the radar of this particular scientist who proceeded to have multiple conversations with the SCP, some indulging it in its delusions of being human and sometimes just being very brutal and pointing out how he's just some poor caricature of humanity without any nuance, eventually the SCP will have a meltdown that will ultimately result into it breaking out of its delusions and slowly remembering it's origins as a being that has been observing our species through the sidelines, and tried to mimic us, using art as a landmark since it was the only consistent thing we did throught our whole history.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber</strong>: I think that an SCP whose abilities are directly connected with art history is quite a fascinating idea, and something that I least think has not been done in this way.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes</strong>: Here are some random concepts based on several critiques I've had</p>
<ul>
<li>Maybe they are very insecure about their art and request feedback and while they say there are open to constructive criticism they really aren't and will try to kill anyone who gives negative feedback</li>
</ul>
<p>View comments for some more details</p>
</div>
</div>
