															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rockteethmotheyes" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4022320); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4022320&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609315137" alt="RockTeethMothEyes" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4022320)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rockteethmotheyes" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4022320); return false;" >RockTeethMothEyes</a></span> <span class="odate time_1609309678 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">30 Dec 2020 06:27</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4857118">
									

<p>A little verbose on the history front, but I think we're getting somewhere.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>humans always found a need to do art, of course there were different kinds of art but it was always art, so it tried to copy us thourhgt the years and believed that replicating our art is the way to comprehend what is &quot;being human&quot; so it currently is in this endless loop it tries to make art</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is probably as close to motivation as we can get; a desire to be human by means of expressing what it believes to be human expressions. The additional &quot;loss of identity&quot; aspect is a bit so-so, but it's workable. This is good!</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I think the narrative of the article could revolve around the scientist breaking it's current delusional state of existence where he is so deep in the whole &quot;Mimicing humans&quot; thing it thinks each one of its forms are actual people with actual life historys, and after that facade is broken they could get him psychological assistance.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I really like this idea! It doesn't necessarily need to be something that the doctor means to do. Maybe they just get fed up with the mistaken identity act and they verbally lash out. You could play with that a little, too; the entity could use the doctor's outrage as it's own inspiration and couple it with realization of what it truly is.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>i plan to write this all way more subtly than here ofc but that's what I have so far</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Subtlety is important, yes, but you should also make sure that you don't sacrifice your core story elements by underplaying them. This is fiction. It is equally important to play up moments to engage the reader.</p>
<p>I'm glad to see that you've taken the time to rethink your approach to this idea. I'm not sure how much more I can do on the brainstorming side here, so it might be better to see how you've decided to execute it. Consider this a <strong><span style="color: green">greenlight</span></strong>. You do need to two to use the Drafts Forums, so if that is something you'd like to pursue, I suggest reaching out to another reviewer, perhaps by utilizing our <a href="/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad Roster</a>.</p>
<p>Good luck.</p>
</div>
</div>
